WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.669
Testing ORM safety means testing both data correctness and security
boundaries.

2
00:00:04.669 --> 00:00:11.571
Unit tests can cover data-access functions, dynamic filter mappings,
serializer field lists, and validation helpers.

3
00:00:11.571 --> 00:00:20.029
Integration tests can confirm that ORM queries, raw SQL paths, migrations,
and transactions behave correctly against a representative database.

4
00:00:20.029 --> 00:00:27.405
Authorization tests should verify model access for normal users,
privileged users, tenants, organizations, and denied cases.

5
00:00:27.405 --> 00:00:31.939
Negative tests are especially valuable for dynamic filters and unsafe
fields.

6
00:00:31.939 --> 00:00:44.119
They can confirm that unsupported sort fields are rejected, that clients
cannot write read-only attributes, that cross-tenant access fails, and
that generic serializers do not expose sensitive relationships.

7
00:00:44.119 --> 00:00:52.103
Regression tests should be added after query fixes so a future feature
does not reintroduce overbroad access or unsafe query construction.

8
00:00:52.103 --> 00:00:57.179
Safe query logging supports investigation without exposing secrets or
sensitive data.

9
00:00:57.179 --> 00:01:04.148
Logs should avoid credentials, tokens, raw connection strings, unnecessary
personal data, and sensitive query values.

10
00:01:04.148 --> 00:01:13.013
Correlation identifiers, high-level event categories, and controlled audit
fields are usually more useful than dumping entire queries with all
values.

11
00:01:13.013 --> 00:01:21.809
Monitoring unusual database access patterns, large exports, repeated
denied access, and unexpected admin queries can help identify problems
earlier.

12
00:01:21.809 --> 00:01:24.922
Code review questions should follow the ORM boundary.

13
00:01:24.922 --> 00:01:26.614
Does this query use safe APIs?

14
00:01:26.614 --> 00:01:28.576
Are dynamic choices allowlisted?

15
00:01:28.576 --> 00:01:32.433
Is authorization included before records are returned or changed?

16
00:01:32.433 --> 00:01:34.057
Are tenant filters present?

17
00:01:34.057 --> 00:01:36.290
Are create and update fields explicit?

18
00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:38.591
Does serialization minimize exposure?

19
00:01:38.591 --> 00:01:40.688
Are raw SQL and migrations reviewed?

20
00:01:40.688 --> 00:01:46.440
ORM safety must be maintained as models, relationships, APIs, reports, and
background jobs evolve.
